exists su name radio song name prompt ob text quoted.text.You are naming a song. The sheet below is the song: its words, its sections, and the phrase it repeats in every chorus.

Give the name of the song.
- Two to eight words.
- The name is the phrase the song repeats, shortened to its heart: the words that carry the meaning, with the rest left out.
- A name of the house looks like "Polish the Armour of Light" or "Every Walk One in Christ": a few words taken from the song itself, carrying the whole meaning.
- Title case: every word opens with a capital, except the small words (a, an, the, and, or, of, in, to, for, with, as, at, by, on, from) unless they are the first or the last word.
- Use the words of the song itself.
- The name is not a sentence, not a description of the song, and not a summary of its teaching.
- No quotation marks, no explanation, no trailing punctuation.
- Plain text only, one line..text.quoted be text ya

